@page "/meet"

<PageTitle>Hot Tub Tri Machine | Meet</PageTitle>

<div class="page-container">
    <section class="page-intro">
        <h3>Meet Your Dynamic Duo</h3>
        <img src="images/hostprofile.png" alt="Hosts" />
        <p>
            Welcome to the chaotic energy of Ursula and the Beast—two personalities as different as a perfectly planned training regimen and a spontaneous trail run.
        </p>
        <p>
            Together, they've logged more miles than most people drive cars, survived more sports nutrition experiments than should be legal, and somehow convinced each other that jumping into a hot tub after a brutal workout is a good idea.
        </p>
        <p>
            Whether they're debating the merits of different training splits, recounting hilarious race day mishaps, or just making each other laugh until someone snorts their coffee, one thing's certain: this podcast is equal parts inspiration, perspiration, and pure entertainment.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="characters-section">
        <div class="characters-grid">
            <!-- Ursula Profile -->
            <div class="character-card">
                <div class="character-image">
                    <img src="images/ursula.png" alt="Ursula" />
                </div>
                <div class="character-content">
                    <h3>Ursula</h3>
                    <p class="character-role">The Encourager</p>
                    <p class="character-bio">
                        <b>Ursula</b> discovered triathlon in 2018 after being diagnosed with Hashimoto's disease and finding a renewed energy for exercise. What started with a swim quickly became a passion for the sport and the incredible sense of achievement that comes from crossing a finish line. A proud back-of-the-pack athlete, she's all about consistency over speed, embracing the challenge, and helping others realise that you don't need to be fast to belong. Whether she's chasing a new personal best, dreaming of one day hearing "Ursula, you are an Ironman," or encouraging fellow athletes to simply keep going, she believes triathlon is for everyone willing to give it a try.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- The Beast Profile -->
            <div class="character-card">
                <div class="character-image">
                    <img src="images/beast.png" alt="The Beast" />
                </div>
                <div class="character-content">
                    <h3>The Beast</h3>
                    <p class="character-role">The Adventurer</p>
                    <p class="character-bio">
                        <b>The Beast</b> came to triathlon through a love of long bike rides and the simple idea that having a goal makes exercise meaningful. Equal parts storyteller, cycling enthusiast and eternal optimist, she believes endurance sport is less about podiums and more about resilience, adventure and finding joy in the process. Known for her self-deprecating humour, love of long rides and confidence on a downhill, she's proof that you don't have to be the fastest athlete on the course to earn your place there. Her mission is simple: help everyday triathletes feel seen, included and inspired to keep training for a healthier, happier life.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

